  "commemorated_topic": "100 Years of the ANZAC Spirit",
  "comments": "This Commemorative coin was issued into circulation each year over a five year period in 2014, 2015, 2016, 2017 &amp; 2018. The coin celebrates 100 Years of ANZAC - Australian and New Zealand Army Corps.<br /><br />\r\nIn addition to being released into general circulation it was available as follows ...<br />\r\nThe 2014 dated coin was available in a Coincard with (M) Melbourne and (AL) Albany Counterstamps.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d8cb33f54d55.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d8cb33f54d55.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"215\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5d8cb350068be.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5d8cb350068be.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"202\" /></a><br />\r\n<span style=\"font-weight:bold;\">The coin on this Numista page above is one with an Albany Counterstamp.</span><br /><br />\r\nThe 2014 dated coin was also issued in PNC Issue 5 of 2014 by Australia Post<br />\r\nIt was also issued in a special limited edition PNC at the Brisbane ANDA Show<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd6238a5d409.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd6238a5d409.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"111\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd62396ee264.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd62396ee264.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"112\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThe low mintage 2016 coin was also issued in a PNC by Australia Post.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd624b1af982.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd624b1af982.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"117\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5dd624bc5349c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5dd624bc5349c.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"117\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThe 2015 dated coin was available in various RAM coin swap events in bags of 10 coins<br />\r\nThe 2015 dated coin was available with a Changeover Tour (MAP) Counterstamp in the shape of Australia<br />\r\nThe 2016 dated coin was available with a Changeover Tour (MAP) Counterstamp in the shape of Australia<br />\r\nThe 2017 dated coin was available in various RAM coin swap events in bags of 10 coins<br />\r\nThe 2018 dated coin was available in various RAM coin swap events in bags of 10 coins<br />\r\nThe 2018 dated coin was available in a small coincard with an (AL) Albany Counterstamp<br /><br />\r\nAll Five years (2014,5,6,7&amp;8) were issued in a special &quot;Spirit Lives&quot; 5 Coin set in 2018.<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5de1e59c2767b.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5de1e59c2767b.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"161\" /></a> <a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5de1e5a6655e0.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5de1e5a6655e0.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"92\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nThere have been reports of a possible Mule coin dated 2014 which has a 10 cent Obverse.",
